TinyCDI — Written Offer for Corresponding Source (GPL-2.0)
=========================================================

The TinyCDI runtime container images (linux-desktop, browser)
redistribute the KasmVNC 1.5.0 server binaries
(kasmvncserver_bookworm_1.5.0_amd64.deb, sha256
770fd3df51510beecc89666879d82faf411276e68c6e11df612f736b891b5f71),
which are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.0.

Written offer
-------------

TinyOrbit offers to provide to any third party, for a charge no more
than the cost of physically performing source distribution (free of
charge for electronic delivery), a machine-readable copy of the
complete corresponding source code for the KasmVNC 1.5.0 binaries
shipped in these images.

The corresponding source — the KasmVNC v1.5.0 source tree including the
kasmweb/noVNC submodule commit it records, plus the third-party sources
upstream's build scripts fetch and statically link (xorg-server,
libjpeg-turbo, libwebp, oneTBB, libcpuid, fmt, libyuv), each pinned by
sha256/commit — is assembled by hack/kasmvnc-source-bundle.sh in this
repository and published with each release as
kasmvnc-1.5.0-corresponding-source.tar.gz together with a .sha256
checksum file.

To exercise this offer, open an issue at
https://github.com/tinyorbitvn/tinycdi/issues (security-sensitive
requests may instead use the repository's GitHub private vulnerability
reporting channel). No postal address is required.

This offer is valid for at least three years from the date each image
is published and applies to anyone who received the image.

Debian packages
---------------

The runtime images are built on Debian 12 (bookworm). Corresponding
source for the Debian packages they contain is available from the
Debian archive via deb-src entries for the bookworm suite at
deb.debian.org; package names and versions are recorded in the image
SBOMs.
